 ## Overview
-4D Neural Voxel Splatting (4D-NVS) is a dynamic scene rendering method that combines voxel-based representations with neural Gaussian splatting to decouple spatial structure from temporal dynamics [S1]. Unlike static methods like Scaffold-GS or methods that replicate Gaussians across time, 4D-NVS generates time-varying Gaussians on-demand from persistent voxel anchors using a unified deformation field, reducing memory complexity from $O(N \cdot T)$ to $O(fV + F)$ [S1]. This approach enables real-time rendering of dynamic scenes with significantly lower memory consumption and faster training times compared to existing radiance-field optimization techniques [S1].
+4D Neural Voxel Splatting (4D-NVS) is a dynamic scene rendering method that combines voxel-based representations with neural Gaussian splatting to decouple spatial structure from temporal dynamics [S1]. It generates neural Gaussians on-demand from persistent voxel anchors and applies unified deformations via a HexPlane encoder, reducing memory complexity to $O(fV + F)$ compared to the $O(N \cdot T)$ scaling of replicating Gaussians across timestamps [S1]. Unlike Scaffold-GS which generates static Gaussians, 4D-NVS produces time-varying Gaussians through learned temporal features, enabling real-time rendering with significantly lower memory consumption [S1].
 
